      "topic": "staff",
      "sentiment": "positive",
      "mentions": 26,
      "title": {
        "en": "Caring and welcoming team"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "The vast majority of reviewers praise the whole team — receptionists, nurses, and vets — as friendly, caring, and never rushing appointments. Several long-term clients mention coming from far away or staying loyal for decades. Nervous animals are consistently described as being handled gently and patiently, and owners feel listened to."
      }
    },
    {
      "topic": "animals",
      "sentiment": "positive",
      "mentions": 10,
      "title": {
        "en": "Gentle handling of anxious pets"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Multiple reviewers specifically bring anxious or difficult-to-handle animals — dogs prone to aggression, nervous cats, elderly pets — and report that staff manage them calmly and with evident affection. Home visits for end-of-life care are mentioned. Owners feel confident their pets are treated with respect and kindness at every stage."
      }
    },
    {
      "topic": "results",
      "sentiment": "mixed",
      "mentions": 11,
      "title": {
        "en": "Generally good outcomes, some concerns"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Most owners are satisfied with treatment results — including complex cases and holistic approaches that avoided antibiotics. However, a few recent reviewers raise concerns: one describes a surgical error (retained ovary), another reports a significant drop in care quality since a change in ownership. These cases represent a minority but are worth noting."
      }
    }
  ],
